This is a great UI/UX improvement. Right now, there is actually a bug in your code: your snackbar message *says* it allows / & ( ) , . -, but the regular expression you are using (/[^a-zA-Z0-9 ]/g) is strictly deleting all of those special characters!
Additionally, swapping out a helpful description for a red error message is jarring for the user. We want the helper text to permanently display exactly what is allowed, while the input physically blocks them from typing anything else.
Here is how to fix the logic, update the regex to actually allow those special characters, and make the UI much smoother.
### Step 1: Update the filterAndWarn Function
Find your existing filterAndWarn function (around line 250) and replace it with this completely fixed version. It will now properly allow the special characters, block the bad ones, and show the snackbar cleanly.
**REPLACE WITH THIS:**
```javascript
  const filterAndWarn = (val) => {
    let filtered = val;
    let hasError = false;
    let msg = "Only alphanumeric, spaces, and / & ( ) , . - are allowed.";

    // 1. Corrected Regex: Allows Alphanumeric, Spaces, and / & ( ) , . -
    const invalidCharRegex = /[^a-zA-Z0-9 \/&(),.\-]/g;
    
    if (invalidCharRegex.test(filtered)) {
      hasError = true;
      filtered = filtered.replace(invalidCharRegex, "");
    }

    // 2. Strip leading space and collapse double spaces
    const beforeSpaceTrim = filtered;
    filtered = filtered.replace(/^\s+/, "").replace(/\s{2,}/g, " ");
    
    if (beforeSpaceTrim !== filtered && !hasError) {
      hasError = true;
      msg = "Remark should not start with a space or contain consecutive spaces.";
    }

    if (hasError) {
      showSnackBar(msg, "warning");
    }
    
    return filtered;
  };

```
